\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2013\par 02:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.1200-6.1237   6.1159-6.1315 \par USD/TWD    29.930-30.000   29.850-30.040 \par USD/KRW     1,116-1,120     1,112-1,123 \par USD/SGD    1.2732-1.2785   1.2700-1.2800 \par USD/MYR    3.2730-3.3000   3.2500-3.3240 \par USD/THB     31.30-31.49     31.20-31.69 \par USD/PHP          -               - \par USD/IDR    10,400-10,500   10,260-10,540 \par USD/INR     63.00-63.22     62.50-63.50 \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY - consolidation with downside bias. Spot USD/CNY is likely to drift back down after Monday's late spike resolved lower eventually, keeping the pair firmly within the Bollinger downtrend channel. A stable USD index likely means the PBOC USD/CNY parity rate will stay close to 6.1690. Investors are still positive on the yuan, though their expectations of the pace of appreciation have been trimmed greatly due to fear of the U.S. Federal Reserve tightening monetary stimulus. PBOC governor Zhou said Monday that there is unlikely the need for major shift in monetary policy, but that more reforms might be coming to the financial sector. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1200 (psychological support), then at 6.1159 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1090 (Friday's record low). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1237 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1315 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 6.1393 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD - consolidation. USD/TWD is likely to remain trapped by the daily Ichimoku Cloud zone that spans 29.850-30.040. The 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line meets the Cloud top at 30.040, adding to the strength of the technical trading barrier, and will likely keep a lid on the dollar. A close proxy to the yuan - which continues to appreciate gradually - the Taiwan dollar's value is hence unlikely to erode much despite the broad rally of the greenback. Taiwan releases its July exports data as well as Balance of Payments numbers later. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.930 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.850 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 29.800 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), then at 30.040 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.180 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW - likely upside bias. The dollar gaps up significantly to 1,119.5 from a Monday closing of 1,115.6, in reaction to another rally in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield. The USD/KRW could take on a more bullish bias if it ends Tuesday above 1,120 - where the Bollinger uptrend channel begins. From there, the greenback could go on to challenge the Ichimoku Cloud hovering nearby at 1,123. Expectations are high for the Fed to begin tapering monetary stimulus next month, and the release of the FOMC minutes tomorrow could confirm this belief. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,116 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1,112 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,110 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1,120 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,123 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 1,124 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD - upside bias. USD/SGD is now well within the Bollinger uptrend channel and also above the daily Ichimoku Cloud - together creating a fairly bullish signal that could propel the pair toward its year-high of 1.2859. The greenback rallied overnight as \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bonds were sold off again, sending the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield up and the dollar along with it. The rally of the U.S. dollar could intensify after Wednesday's release of the U.S. Federal Reserve's July meeting minutes - which could show the Fed leaning towards tapering in September. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2732 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2700 (psychological support), before 1.2691 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2785 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), before 1.2859 (2013 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR - upside bias. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel continues to pull USD/MYR upwards, potentially to the major psychological trading barrier at 3.3000. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the pace of ringgit depreciation, and may even attempt to draw a line in the sand near 3.3000 as the ringgit is already at a 3-year low. Confidence in the Malaysia ringgit is shaky as the market awaits the release of Balance of Payments data Wednesday, which might show the country falling into a current account deficit for the first time since 1997. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2730 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2500 (psychological support), before 3.2460 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3000 (major psychological barrier), then at 3.3010 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3240 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB - upside bias. USD/THB has entered the Bollinger uptrend channel at 31.30 and is now on track toward the channel ceiling at 31.49, implying more baht weakness to come. The baht is under pressure not just because of broad greenback strength, but also because Thailand's GDP fell for the second quarter in a row, data released Tuesday showed, signalling a mild technical recession. The government has trimmed its forecast for full-year growth to 3.8%-4.3% from its previous estimate of 4.2%-5.2%. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 31.30 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.20 (psychological support), before 31.11 (20-day Bollinger mid and Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 31.49 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 31.50 (psychological resistance), before 31.69 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP - closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR - upside bias. USD/IDR may notch another 4-year high as Indonesia assets collapse under pressure from the country's slowing growth, high inflation and widening current account deficit. Stocks in Jakarta fell 5.6% Monday, and could continue Tuesday as panicked investors rush for the exit. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  last Thursday said the risk of slowing growth "remains significant". Southeast Asia's biggest economy expanded 5.8% in the second quarter, its slowest pace since 2010. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 10,400 (psychological support), then at 10,260 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 10,200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 10,500 (psychological resistance), before 10,540 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR - upside bias. The rupee could continue falling as no clear support levels are in sight because the USD/INR is in uncharted territory again. Yet another historical high of 63.22 was set Monday, a sign that the market is not convinced by the government's recent moves to buffer the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The rupee has been a on streak of record-setting losses this month, and the government can't seem to rein it in despite various measures to lower the current account deficit and simultaneously making it more expensive for banks to short the rupee. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 63.00 (psychological support), then at 62.50 (psychological support), before 62.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 63.22 (record high), before 63.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 20-08-13 0035GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130820e98k0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
