\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia-Market factors to watch Feb 20\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2012\par 01:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Following is a list of events in Malaysia as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets. Reuters News welcomes your feedback and for any queries, please contact the Kuala Lumpur newsroom at +603 2333 8046 or via email at areuters@gmail.com\par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN MALAYSIA, TIMES LOCAL FOLLOWED BY GMT: (The inclusion of diary items does not necessarily mean that Reuters will cover the event). > Thai Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra's one-day official visit in Malaysia. > The New Toyota Prius & The All-New Toyota Prius media launch at Sunway Pyramid Convention Centre, Bandar Sunway, Petaling Jaya at 2.30pm (0630). > Plantation Industries and Commodities Minister Bernard Dompok and Agriculture and Agro-based Industry Minister Noh Omar launch the use of B5 biodiesel for Fisheries Sector at Jeti Nelayan Bagan Pasir, Tanjung Karang at 10.00am (0200). > Prime Minister Najib Razak receives courtesy call from Thai Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra at Prime Minister's Office, Putrajaya at 3.00pm (0700), and attends closed-door meeting with Thai Prime Minister Yongluck Shinawatra at 3.30pm (0730). > Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signing ceremony and joint press conference at Prime Minister's office, Putrajaya at 5.00pm (0900). > Prime Minister Najib Razak hosts official dinner in conjunction with Thai Prime Minister Yingluck Shinawatra visit at Seri Perdana, Putrajaya at 8.25pm (1225).\par \par \uc2 MARKET SNAPSHOT: * Malaysia's benchmark stock index dropped 0.43 percent on Friday. Leading movers were the country's power firm Tenaga Nasional which dropped 1.83 percent, while lender Hong Leong Financial rose 1.73 percent. * U.S. stocks edged higher on Friday, but investors stayed cautious before a long holiday weekend when hopes are set for Greece's bailout plan to be approved. * World stocks hit a 6-1/2-month peak and the euro gained on Friday on hopes that Greece will next week seal a long-awaited bailout deal needed to avert a disorderly debt default.\par \par \uc2 * Malaysian crude palm oil futures climbed to a near two-month high on Friday on hopes that Greece will soon secure a bailout package, while dry weather fears in soy-producing South America also provided support. * To see Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regular money market tenders issued at around 0930 local please click on the following link {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fast.bnm.gov.my/fastweb/public/MainPage.do?mode=MAIN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fast.bnm.gov.my/fastweb/public/MainPage.do?mode=MAIN}}}\uc2  * For a political risk box on Malaysia, click on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/Risks/Malaysia.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://graphics.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/Risks/Malaysia.pdf}}}\par \par \uc2 * For Asian weekly risks, click on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/jum59n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/jum59n}}}\par \par \uc2 IN THE NEWS REUTERS MALAYSIA (Click on ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par > Gas Malaysia's IPO delays to second quarter                     \par > Asia Cocoa-Butter ratios above 1.0; mid-crop harvest nears end  \tab \par > Thai rubber \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  scheme delayed to March                \tab \par > \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  upgrades Taiwan, Indonesia, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2              \tab \par > Malaysia's CIMB to buy RBS' Australian assets for $50 mln-paper \tab \par > Malaysia's Maxis plans $801 million sukuk                       \tab \par > POLL-Investors slash Sing dlr bets, halve Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 