\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Greece hopes lift Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , but  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caps\b0\par\par\uc2 1,084 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2012\par 05:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Taiwan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Philippine c.banks spotted -dealers\par \par \uc2  * Stock inflows lift Taiwan dlr, won\par \par \uc2  * Rating upgrade bets support Philippine peso \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 8 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Wednesday, driven by capital inflows and demand from offshore funds as investors remained hopeful that Greece will strike a debt restructuring deal, but local investors remained wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional authorities.\par \par \uc2  Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars to cap its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains, while Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may also be in the market, dealers said. This comes at a time when many emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are approaching major resistance levels.\par \par \uc2  The outlook for regional units remains firm, given improved risk appetite, and they are expected to break through resistance levels if Greece succeeds in securing a 130 billion euro ($170 billion) rescue fund, analysts and dealers said.\par \par \uc2  Even though Greece is seen close to an agreement, its politicians have yet to accept to painful austerity measures to receive the second bailout package. They have delayed, once more, the deal deadline to Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Asian central banks are also likely to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and slow the rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help support weakening exports, they added.\par \par \uc2  "The strength in Asia ex-Japan (\b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is impressive considering the state of the global economy, though momentum seems to be improving. Thus \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to be expected," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Scotia Capital in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2  "I just can't get the euro zone out of my head. I think one should trade with the trend, but remain vigilant as it could turn should Greece give us negative headlines," he added.\par \par \uc2  Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have risen this year, thanks to resumed foreign inflows amid high liquidity and growing hopes that the euro zone's debt crisis is easing.\par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar/Taiwan dollar slid on stock inflows, while Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and importers supported the pair, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's demand for the greenback was relatively small around the current levels, but many local banks were lined up to buy the pair between 29.40 and 29.45, they add.\par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were net buyers in Taiwan stock market in the previous two sessions and market has had net inflows of T$15.7 billion ($531.24 million) so far this month until Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  Dollar/won fell on selling by offshore funds and custodian, but its slide is limited as investors stay wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2  The pair has a support line at 1,110, around a 200-day moving average.\par \par \uc2  Investors are keeping an eye on demand linked to Lone Star's sale of a stake in \uc2 Korea Exchange Bank\uc2  (KEB) to \uc2 Hana Financial Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  A market source said the U.S. private equity fund appears to still need to buy some $900 million.\par \par \uc2  "Everybody is reluctant to sell dollars here. So, even though dollar/won is seen sliding more, but it would be very slow," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  Still, some dealers see low possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the country remains wary of inflation.\par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  Dollar/baht breached a support line at 30.80, near the 50 percent Fibonacci retracement of its July-January rise.\par \par \uc2  The pair is expected to fall further, given improved risk appetite, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "A trend is very clear for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so market is waiting to sell (USD/THB) on rally," said a Bangkok-based dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/baht may head to 30.67, the low of December. The next level would be 30.50, around the 61.8 percent retracement.\par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2  Dollar/Philippine peso fell on inflows, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying the pair, dealer said.\par \par \uc2  "Especially after IDR got upgraded, punters are looking to PHP to be the next," said a Singapore-based dealer, referring to Indonesia's sovereign rating upgrade last month.\par \par \uc2  Remittance inflows are expected to put more pressure on the pair, the dealer added.\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying the pair around 42.30 initially, but lowered the bid level to around 42.20, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  RINGGIT\par \par \uc2  Dollar/ringgit hit a five-month low on catch-up plays after holidays, falling to as low as 2.9950, the first time to breach the 3.0000 level since Sept 9.\par \par \uc2  Some dealers suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of buying dollars to defend the 3.0000 support line, around the 76.4 percent retracement level at 2.9983 of its July-October rise.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0735 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.10          76.77       -0.43\par  Sing dlr        1.2432         1.2455       +0.19\par  Taiwan dlr      29.503         29.570       +0.23\par  Korean won     1115.00        1118.70       +0.33\par  Baht             30.73          30.92       +0.62\par  Peso             42.24          42.41       +0.40\par  Rupiah         8985.00        8935.00       -0.56\par  Rupee            49.05          49.19       +0.30\par  Ringgit         3.0005         3.0115       +0.37\par  Yuan            6.2957         6.3049       +0.15\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.10          76.92       -0.24\par  Sing dlr        1.2432         1.2969       +4.32\par  Taiwan dlr      29.503         30.290       +2.67\par  Korean won     1115.00        1151.80       +3.30\par  Baht             30.73          31.55       +2.67\par  Peso             42.24          43.84       +3.79\par  Rupiah         8985.00        9060.00       +0.83\par  Rupee            49.05          53.08       +8.23\par  Ringgit         3.0005         3.1685       +5.60\par  Yuan            6.2957         6.2940       -0.03\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \tab \par (Additional reporting by Reuters \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analyst Krishna Kumar in\par SYDNEY, Yingchien Lee in TAIPEI, Lee Shin-hyung in SEOUL and\par Catherine Tan of IFR Markets; Editing by Kim Coghill)\tab \