\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Indonesian Shares End +1.1%; 3750 Cap Eyed Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2011\par 11:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0928 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian shares end up 1.1% at 3727.798 in moderate volume, led by foreigners' bargain-buying in most bank, commodity- and consumer-related stocks after recent falls, traders say; they tip the main index to top 3750. "I expect foreign funds will continue to buy on hopes for strong first-quarter earnings" in most companies, says a trader with BNI Securities. Foreigners are net buyers of IDR154 billion worth of shares. Among gainers: car maker Astra (ASII.JK) is up 2.6% at IDR58,100, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Mandiri\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BMRI.JK) is up 2.3% at IDR6,800, while coal producer Bumi (BUMI.JK) is up 3.2% at IDR3,275. (edhi.pranasidhi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [Dow Jones] Sonia rates still suggest the Bank of England will raise rates 25 bps in July and then again in November, after U.K. manufacturing output came in with a flat reading for February versus expectations of a 0.7% rise. "Although there is a danger of reading too much into one month's data, a number of other indicators show that the recovery is in a tenuous state," says Hetal Mehta at Daiwa Capital Markets. "Any chance of an interest rate hike in May, let alone tomorrow, has diminished markedly." June gilts are up 0.25 at 116.83. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0917 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/JPY is one of the stand out charts Wednesday says \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  with the cross on the cusp of reversing the long-term trend for JPY appreciation which has been in place since 2008. The bank says a break above 122.30 will target 127.95 with a weekly close above the cloud-cap at 121.95 opening potential for 139.00 later in 2011. Now at 121.53. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0916 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is lower at 8,650 vs 8,660 late Tuesday due to capital inflows to the local stock and bond markets as risk appetite improves globally, say dealers; but they add that further falls will likely be limited as the market is already short on the dollar. "The dollar's slide is losing steam as it's already oversold," says a dealer. Three dealers say Bank Indonesia was suspected of buying around $50 million at the 8,650 level to slow the pair's fall. They tip a 8,645-8,665 range for Thursday. Indonesia shares ended 1.1% higher. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0911 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares end flat with the KLCI closing down 0.18 points at 1552.89; a local dealer says there was some profit-taking in select blue-chips and construction stocks after their recent rally. "The market is somewhat overbought with the recent rally that took the index close to its all-time high, so some consolidation is expected." He tips immediate support at 1545, followed by 1537, the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement of the recent 1474 low to the 1576 record high; the Monday high of 1565.04 will likely act as strong resistance. Market breadth is positive with 489 gainers vs 310 losers. Among gainers Genting Malaysia (4715.KU) rose 2.4% at MYR3.77, \uc2 Genting Bhd\uc2  (3182.KU) was up 1.8% at MYR11.22 and \uc2 MAA Holdings\uc2  (1198.KU) added 22.4% to MYR1.20 on a New Straits Times report it may sell its insurance unit to Zurich Insurance. Among losers, \uc2 IOI Corp\uc2 . (1961.KU) lost 3.0% to MYR5.55 and Gamuda (5398.KU) was off 0.8% at MYR3.87. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0857 GMT [Dow Jones] US Treasurys are little changed in light European trading, a trader says. "Volumes are low and the range is tight. There is plenty for the market to think about, but its coming further down the line." Fed hawk Bullard's comments that he will push for a $100 billion cut in the quantitative easing program are outweighed by Bernanke's commitment on seeing the program through. "The FOMC minutes at the end of the month will be crucial, but there's nothing like that to focus on near-term, except the ECB," the trader adds. 10-year Treasury yields are flat at 3.48% and the June contract is up 0.05 at 118-250. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0853 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP hit a 5-month low late Wednesday, weighed by equity-related inflows, remittances from overseas Filipino workers, and also as the EUR advances against the USD. The pair is at 43.13 from 43.35 late Tuesday in heavy volume. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprisingly allowed the dollar/peso to breach the 43.25 major support, so we're expecting further downside tomorrow," says a local bank trader. He tips next support at 42.90 with resistance at 43.25. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0846 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts rise after UK manufacturing data come in weaker than expected. Manufacturing output in February was flat on the month vs expectations for a 0.7% rise. June gilts are up 0.16 at 116.74 vs 116.59 before the data. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0845 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/INR is down, but off the nearly six-month low touched earlier in the session, on custodial flows, says a senior dealer with a foreign bank. The pair is at 44.23 after falling as low as 44.175, last touched on Oct. 18, compared with 44.43 late Tuesday. "Apart from the flows, the euro and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like the Korean won, have strengthened, which is helping the INR. Though 44.18-44.20 levels are presenting a good buying opportunity for oil-importing companies," he says. He expects the pair in a broad range of 44.15-44.30 for the rest of the session. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] Before its Swiss CPI-fueled collapse early Wednesday, the future looked bright for EUR/CHF. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst Karen Jones says with the cross breaching its 200-day MA at 1.3145 and also overcoming the 1.3205 February high, a close below here Wednesday evening in Europe, would set the rate up for a move toward the 1.3445 Fibonacci level. However after Swiss March CPI came in at double the 0.5% forecast, EUR/CHF plummeted to 1.3096 from around 1.3220. It now trades at 1.31073. Jones pegs support at 1.3045 ahead of 1.30 and 1.2965 and still favors the upside while the cross trades above 1.2920. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/MYR is a tad lower at 3.0240 vs late Tuesday's level of 3.0250; two traders say \uc2 Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at both the 3.0240 and 3.0250 levels. A local trader adds, "if the Singapore dollar is allowed to appreciate, maybe Malaysia will follow suit with the MYR. Our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been tracking the Singapore dollar and will likely continue doing that." He tips a 3.0240-3.0300 range for Thursday, with a 2-month target of 3.0150.(ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling falls to the day's low against many of its peers after February's industrial output data showed a surprise 1.2% month on month fall against an expected 0.5% increase. GBP/USD drops to 1.6282 from around 1.6340, EUR/GBP climbs to 0.8778 from 0.8757 while GBP/JPY hits 138.23 for a 150sen loss on the day and GBP/CHF is also 150 ticks off its 1.5186 day high. (gary.stride@dowjones.com) [ 04-06-11 0528ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022  \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110406e7460006e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
