\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/MYR Tad Down;3.0240-3.0300 Range Tipped Thursday\b0\par\par\uc2 1,329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2011\par 10:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0841 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/MYR is a tad lower at 3.0240 vs late Tuesday's level of 3.0250; two traders say \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Malaysia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market at both the 3.0240 and 3.0250 levels. A local trader adds, "if the Singapore dollar is allowed to appreciate, maybe Malaysia will follow suit with the MYR. Our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been tracking the Singapore dollar and will likely continue doing that." He tips a 3.0240-3.0300 range for Thursday, with a 2-month target of 3.0150.(ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling falls to the day's low against many of its peers after February's industrial output data showed a surprise 1.2% month on month fall against an expected 0.5% increase. GBP/USD drops to 1.6282 from around 1.6340, EUR/GBP climbs to 0.8778 from 0.8757 while GBP/JPY hits 138.23 for a 150sen loss on the day and GBP/CHF is also 150 ticks off its 1.5186 day high. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0839 GMT [Dow Jones] HUF strengthens further versus EUR as investors are confident in Hungary's prospective fiscal prudence, one trader says. HUF adds to its gains as markets have already priced in the ECB's likely rate increase, Thursday, which would slightly narrow Hungary's rate advantage versus the euro zone. EUR/HUF is at 263.61 from 264.03 late Tuesday, last time HUF was this strong was April 2010. Raiffeisen Bank trader Matyas Kovacs sees further short-term HUF firming, with EUR/HUF possibly breaking support at 262. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0837 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD pares some of its losses late Wednesday, after Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 29.024 level in the afternoon, say two local traders; the pair is at 29.150 from 29.000 earlier and compared with 29.320 late Friday. "The (suspected) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were quite mild...I guess the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  just doesn't want the Taiwan dollar to rise too fast, and is not aiming to push it lower," says one of the traders. Another trader adds, "if the stock market continues to be this buoyant, (the pair) could easily fall below 29.00." She tips the pair to hover in 28.95-29.10 range Thursday. The Taiex ended up 1.7% at its highest closing level in nearly two months; foreign investors' net buy totaled NT$22.22 billion. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 ("MARKET TALK: PLN May Strengthen More After Rate Rise - BZ WBK," at 0823 GMT, misstated the relevance of CPI data to domestic interest rates. The correct version follows:)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty may strengthen some more after domestic interest rates rose by 25 basis points Tuesday, says \uc2 Bank Zachodni WBK\uc2 . EUR/PLN may approach 3.975 on Wednesday after the MPC published a hawkish statement after raising rates, Zachodni WBK adds. Polish rates may go up twice more this year by a total of 50 basis points, the brokerage says. EUR/PLN is at 3.9893 from 3.9923 late Tuesday, USD/PLN at 2.7901 from 2.8075. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0829 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesian government bond prices continue to rally, as capital inflows continue amid improving risk appetite, dealers say. "Yields could continue sliding for the rest of the week if inflows persist, but the slide will likely slow as bond prices are already expensive," a dealer says; the five-year yield is down at 7.20% from 7.24% late Tuesday, the 10-year yield edges down to 7.71% from 7.73%, the 15-year yield falls to 8.89% from 8.55% and the 20-year yield edges down to 8.89% from 9.01%. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0827 GMT [Dow Jones]--Solid Czech industrial output and foreign trade surplus data for February bear little relevance for the monetary policy of the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or CNB, which remains more concerned about a timid consumer demand, adjusted for a year-on-year spike in car sales, says Martin Lobotka, an economist at the Czech unit of \uc2 Erste Group Bank\uc2 . "Although the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Tuesday) raised its rates and the ECB may decide to do the same tomorrow, we still believe that Czechs don't have to follow them," Lobotka says, adding that the koruna is still stronger than the zloty and marginally firmer than its fundamental value. Even though CNB may make a surprise rate increase as early as May 5, it will more likely delay the interest rate tightening until 3Q, he says. CZK trades a weaker in at 24.409-24.419 against the euro, from 24.35 late Tuesday, tracking similar moves on other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. (leos.rousek@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty may strengthen some more after CPI data Tuesday showed domestic interest rates rose by 25 basis points, says \uc2 Bank Zachodni WBK\uc2 . EUR/PLN may approach 3.975 on Wednesday after the MPC published a hawkish statement after raising rates, Zachodni WBK adds. Polish rates may go up twice more this year by a total of 50 basis points, the brokerage says. EUR/PLN is at 3.9893 from 3.9923 late Tuesday, USD/PLN at 2.7901 from 2.8075. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0818 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia government bonds are mixed late, with some buying in shorter-term paper as foreign funds come in with the recent strength in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a local dealer says. He adds, the focus remains on Bank Negara notes, with more than MYR5.0 billion changing hands. He also says there aren't any real leads, so the market is expected to remain sideways for the near term. The yield on the August 2014 MGS is down 2 bps at 3.41%, the September 2016 MGS yield is up 2 bps at 3.66%, the September 2017 MGS yield is down 1 bp at 3.83%, while the July 2021 MGS yield is unchanged at 4.09%. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Komercni Banka\uc2  traders expect good demand for the Czech sale of CZK7 billion ($407 million) of the 4% April 2017 bonds at auction Wednesday, due to "nice" asset swap spread and good environment for bond holders should generate good demand. Komercni expects a bid-to-cover ratio around 2, and price within the market spread, around +56 in asset swap terms, says trader Dalimil Vyskovsky. Results are due at 1000 GMT. (emese.bartha@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0812 GMT [Dow Jones] Peripheral euro-zone sovereign yield spreads versus Germany are mostly 2 bps-3 bps tighter thanks to the rise in German yields Wednesday. Portugal is the exception, as its 5-year and 10-year spreads to Germany move 2 bps-3 bps wider ahead of an auction of 6-month and 12-month bills that is seen as having no real impact on the country's ability to stave off a bailout. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT [Dow Jones] PLN will benefit in the coming weeks from expectations that after Tuesday's interest rates rise another increase will take place soon, possibly in May or June, says BRE. The MPC will become increasingly concerned with rising inflation pressure in Poland after Thursday's likely rate rise in the euro zone, followed by likely much higher Polish inflation for March and another rise of inflation expectations the panel and the market aren't currently anticipating, BRE adds. EUR/PLN is at 3.9921 from 3.9923 late Tuesday. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com) [ 04-06-11 0441ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110406e7460005t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
