\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Officials slow rising  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  despite inflation threat\b0\par\par\uc2 797 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2011\par 03:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Indonesian, Thai, Philippine, Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted - dealers\par \par \uc2  * Won down on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution, importers\par \par \uc2  * Central banks not comfortable with speed of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains - analysts   (Updates with text, prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 21 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit another 3-1/2-year high against the dollar on Monday and dealers said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars, suggesting authorities were not comfortable with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rapid rise.\par \par \uc2  Central banks of Thailand, the Philippines and \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and to maintain export competitiveness, dealers said, respectively pushing down the baht, peso and the ringgit.\par \par \uc2  The South Korean won was the worst performer on the day among emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on caution over possible dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities, especially as some dealers suspected the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  via the non-deliverable forward market on Friday in New York.\par \par \uc2  The moves by the regional authorities showed their discomfort with the speed of the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, even though stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  help mitigate inflation, analysts said.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not the only tool to curb inflation. Other measures are also important," said Philip Wee, a treasury market strategist with DBS in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  The rupiah has risen 1.6 percent since the Bank Indonesia raised interest rates on Feb 4, which alleviated some worries that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was letting inflation get out of control.\par \par \uc2  RUPIAH\par \par \uc2  The dollar/rupiah  came under pressure from sales by custodian banks and leveraged funds ahead of government bond auctions and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying dollars to check the rupiah's strength, dealers say.\par \par \uc2  The pair fell to as low as 8,840, the lowest since June 2007 and compared with its previous close of 8,855.\par \par \uc2  "State banks (suspected on behalf of the central banks) are actively buying the USD in the market... To anticipate a big flow coming," said an Asian bank dealer based in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2  Finance ministry is looking to raise 5 trillion rupiah ($564.7 million) in a regular bond auction selling one year T-bills plus 5-year, 10-year and 20-year government debt.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The dollar/won  climbed on importer demand for settlements and caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Some local players also covered dollar-short positions.\par \par \uc2  The one-month dollar/won NDF was quoted at 1,117.0/7.5 late on Friday in New York and traded at 1,120.2 as of 0510 GMT.\par \par \uc2  "The authorities appeared to manage the closing price of NDFs last weekend, which implies their strong determination to defend 1,110," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  The dollar/baht  opened at 30.56-30.58 and has given ground right away on catch up selling.\par \par \uc2  It hit low of 30.52 as the \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selliing dollars.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\tab \par   Change on the day at 0610 GMT  \tab \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        83.15          83.04       -0.13\par   Sing dlr        1.2748         1.2730       -0.14\par   Taiwan dlr      29.348         29.408       +0.20\par   Korean won     1117.90        1112.10       -0.52\par   Baht             30.53          30.60       +0.23\par   Peso             43.44          43.34       -0.23\par   Rupiah         8849.00        8855.00       +0.07\par   Rupee            45.14          45.19       +0.12\par   Ringgit         3.0350         3.0330       -0.07\par   Yuan            6.5661         6.5732       +0.11\par                                                                                                \par   Change so far in 2011                                                                    \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        83.15          81.15       -2.41\par   Sing dlr        1.2748         1.2820       +0.56\par   Taiwan dlr      29.348         30.368       +3.48\par   Korean won     1117.90        1134.80       +1.51\par   Baht             30.53          30.14       -1.28\par   Peso             43.44          43.84       +0.92\par   Rupiah         8849.00        9005.00       +1.76\par   Rupee            45.14          44.70       -0.96\par   Ringgit         3.0350         3.0820       +1.55\par   Yuan            6.5661         6.5897       +0.36\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1=8855 Rupiah)\tab \par (Additional reporting by Lee Kyoung-ho in S