\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: China Fixes Yuan At Record High, Setting Tone For Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2011\par 05:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- China fixes the yuan at a record high against the dollar\par \par \uc2 -- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the Korean won, Taiwan dollar and Thai baht rise\par \par \uc2 -- Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotes, context) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Arran Scott \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed the yuan's exchange rate at a record high against the dollar Wednesday, hours after it raised interest rates to cool its economy, setting the tone for a broad rise in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as authorities aim to quell rising inflation pressures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central banks in South Korea and Malaysia were again selling their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for dollars to keep them from rising too quickly, traders said, indicating the authorities are taking care not to damage the export industries crucial to the region's economic growth.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set its parity rate for the dollar at CNY6.5850, down from Tuesday's close of CNY6.5938 in the over-the-counter market and that day's fixing rate of CNY6.5860. China's markets were closed since then for Lunar New Year holidays.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is now up 3.7% since the PBOC ended the yuan's two-year peg to the dollar in mid-June. Trading in yuan derivatives offshore show investors now expect the dollar to fall to 6.4220/6.4270 in the coming year, compared with the 6.4493/6.4728 implied by one-year nondeliverable forwards before the Chinese holidays.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which have marked modest gains so far this year, continued to rise Wednesday. With China playing such a large role in the region's economy, the rest of Asia watches Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy closely, seeking to ensure that their own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  don't rise so much that their exporters become uncompetitive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell against the Taiwan dollar to a fresh 13-year low in early trading, and slipped against the Thai baht. It was also slightly lower against the Korean won, though the Bank of Korea was suspected of buying dollars, Seoul traders said. Against the Malaysian ringgit, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was steady at Tuesday's closing level of MYR3.0330, where two local dealers said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  defended the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "China's rate hike should be good for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the Malaysian ringgit isn't rising because Bank Negara is at the 3.0330 level," said one dealer.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The PBOC raised one-year lending and deposit rates by 25 basis points late Tuesday, to 6.06% and 3.0% respectively, the third hike since October, underscoring policy makers' discomfort with percolating price pressures across the economy. Since the start of 2010, the PBOC has also raised the ratio of deposits that banks must hold in reserve seven times.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation has been picking up in the region, fueled by fast economic growth and soaring prices of food and commodities. In China, consumer prices are expected to keep rising in the first quarter on strong holiday demand and bad weather. The consumer price index rose 4.6% from a year earlier in December, less than November's 5.1% rise, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to be uncomfortable with price pressures and some analysts expect inflation could rise by as high as 6.0% in the first half of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The PBOC was the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia to tighten monetary policy in recent months. Authorities are gradually moving to remove monetary stimulus that helped spur economic recoveries from the global financial crisis but is now adding to inflationary pressures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central banks such as Bank Indonesia have signaled that stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be a tool in the inflation fight, and investors appear to be buying into that notion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The PBOC sets a daily central parity rate for the yuan, allowing the tightly managed local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to move up to 0.5% either way. Yuan/ringgit and yuan/ruble can as much as 5%, while other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are allowed to move as much as 3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4042; arran.scott@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Jean Jung in Shanghai, Aaron Back in Beijing, Min-Jeong Lee in Seoul, Lorraine Luk in Taipei, and Elffie Chew in Kuala Lumpur contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 08, 2011 23:35 ET (04:35 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110209e729000qs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
