\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, peso up on weak dlr; Taiwan  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  spotted\b0\par\par\uc2 908 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2011\par 03:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Won up 0.6 pct, peso up 0.5 pct\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Taiwan, \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spotted\par \par \uc2  * Taiwan c.bank seen defending $T29 vs dollar\par \par \uc2  By Cheon Jong-woo\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 19 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the  Philippine peso led gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday as  investors reduced dollar positions on a broad weakness in the  greenback.\par \par \uc2  Central banks in Taiwan and Malaysia were spotted buying  dollars to cap gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while caution over  \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Seoul also prevented the won from strengthening  past 1,110 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were expected to stay firm as the dollar  index hit a two-month low, breaking through the bottom of the daily ichimoku chart, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "Look at the dollar index chart, a signal that the market is putting on risk," said a Kuala Lumpur-based dealer.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors are keeping an eye on a summit between  China and the United States.\par \par \uc2  Chinese President Hu Jintao arrived in the United States on  Tuesday for a four-day state visit amid U.S. complaints  about Beijing's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. \par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won  rose as one of the country's  shipbuilders announced a big foreign order and market players  cleared dollar-long positions.\par \par \uc2  However, caution grew over possible dollar-buying  \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to stem its  strength.\par \par \uc2  "Few expect the won to strengthen past 1,110, so offshore are not active buyers around this level," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  Another dealer said the won may cut gains if the euro falls  or Seoul shares give up rises.\par \par \uc2  On the corporate front, \uc2 Hyundai Heavy Industries\uc2   said it had won a 1.14 trillion won order to build two drillships from U.S. offshore drilling contractor \uc2 Noble Drilling\uc2 , prompting expectations for more won demand.  \par \par \uc2  PESO\par \par \uc2  The peso gained 0.4 percent on a jump in the euro and with data showing the country's balance of payment last year hit a record high of $14.4 billion. \par \par \uc2  Credit Agricole expects the peso to strengthen to 41.50 per  dollar at the end of this year as worries about the country's  inflation is groundless and on strong current account surplus.\par \par \uc2  Credit Agricole recommended to sell dollar/peso six-month  non-deliverable forwards (NDF).\par \par \uc2  "Worries over inflation seem unfounded as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not behind the curve," it said in a research note. "Monetary  tightening will support the PHP. Strong current account surplus  will put upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2  Credit Agricole said it expects two 25-bps rate hike this  year, which will allow policy makers to keep inflation in check.\par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose 1.5 percent, but stayed  weaker than T$29 per U.S. dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed  many bids for the greenback. That made investors and exporters reluctant to sell the U.S. dollars, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  A trader at a local bank in Taiwan said exporters might only offer more US dollar next week before the China Lunar new year.\par \par \uc2  A Taiwan dollar dealer at a U.S. bank in Singapore said he  expected the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the T$29 for the time being.\par \par \uc2  "The CBC is on the bid, it can decide the rate, not us," he  added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0715 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        82.23          82.59       +0.44\par  Sing dlr        1.2800         1.2825       +0.20\par  Taiwan dlr      29.014*        29.450       +1.50\par  Korean won     1110.45        1116.60       +0.55\par  Baht             30.41          30.45       +0.13\par  Peso             44.32          44.55       +0.52\par  Rupiah         9045.00        9049.00       +0.04\par  Rupee            45.37          45.39       +0.06\par  Ringgit         3.0510         3.0560       +0.16\par  Yuan            6.5820         6.5829       +0.01\par  \par  Change so far in 2011\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        82.23          81.15       -1.31\par  Sing dlr        1.2800         1.2820       +0.16\par  Taiwan dlr      29.014         30.368       +4.67\par  Korean won     1110.45        1134.80       +2.19\par  Baht             30.41          30.14       -0.89\par  Peso             44.32          43.84       -1.08\par  Rupiah         9045.00        9005.00       -0.44\par  Rupee            45.37          44.70       -1.47\par  Ringgit         3.0510         3.0820       +1.02\par  Yuan            6.5820         6.5897       +0.12\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  * The Taiwan dollar rate is not the closing price. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regularly near the end of the \par session to weaken the Taiwanese dollar, causing the daily \par comparisons to look larger.\par  \par  (Additional reporting by Clear Jim in TAIPEI and Cathering Tan \par of IFR Markets; Editing by Alex Richardson)\par  \par  \par  \par  For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please click\par  \par   \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Double click on brackets for following items:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia \par  Malaysian ringgit   Indonesian rupiah  \par  Singapore dollar    Thai baht          \par  Taiwan dollar       Hong Kong dollar   \par  Philippine peso      Korean won         \par  SPEED GUIDES  \par  Exotic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      Non-G7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   \par  RELATED NEWS AND OTHER TOPICS\par  All Singapore news    All Malaysian news \par  Thailand Indonesia Hong Kong Taiwan \par  Philippines Korea All emerging markets \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news    \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  technical analysis    [FRX&INSI]\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|E|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110122e71j00015\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
