\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ: Asian Central Banks  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  as  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2010\par 03:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WSJ: Asian Central Banks \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rise\par \par \uc2 By ARRAN SCOTT, ARIES POON and DITAS LOPEZ\par \par \uc2 Central banks in South Korea, \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Thailand are believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Thursday as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  surged against the dollar on optimism about the region's economic outlook, underscored by strong economic data from China and signals that the yuan will continue to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan, meanwhile, unveiled measures to buttress its banking system against rapid movements in foreign capital, the latest Asian economy to introduce stricter regulations to control the risks posed by such capital flows.\par \par \uc2 Capital has been flooding into Asia this year, helping finance investments in the fast-growing region. But the influx of foreign money has raised concerns in Asian capitals about the perils of fast-moving capital flows, given the damage the region's economies suffered during the Asian financial crisis of the late 1990s when a previous boom ended suddenly and foreigners rushed for the exits.\par \par \uc2 Fresh data Thursday from China, the powerhouse of the Asian economy, showed manufacturing growth eased slightly in December but was still at relatively high levels. The HSBC China Manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index, a gauge of nationwide manufacturing activity, fell to 54.4 in December from 55.3 in November; any reading above 50 indicates expansion.\par \par \uc2 CIMB's Mr. Lum said central banks in emerging markets are looking at tightening monetary policy next year, which means interest-rate differentials between emerging markets and the developed economies of the U.S., Europe and Japan should grow wider. That leaves Asian central banks looking for ways to control inflows of capital chasing higher returns.\par \par \uc2 In Kuala Lumpur, traders said Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying dollars to curb a rise in the ringgit, which hit a three-month high Thursday. \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  may have bought dollars at around 3.0810-3.0820 ringgit per dollar, dealers said. The dollar was at 3.0846 ringgit in late trade.\par \par \uc2 Traders in Seoul said they suspected the Bank of Korea entered the market, buying more than $500 million at several intervals between 1,135 and 1,140 won per dollar. The dollar closed at 1,134.80 won, bringing the won's gains against the dollar to 2.6% for the year.\par \par \uc2 In Bangkok, the dollar was at 30.15 baht in late trade - down from 30.16 baht late Wednesday - with suspected buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  around that level to limit the downside, two dealers said.\par \par \uc2 In Taipei, which has been trying to temper gains in the New Taiwan dollar - a favorite among investors seeking exposure to China, given Taiwan's increasingly close economic ties to the mainland - Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced new measures to control capital flows.\par \par \uc2 Starting Saturday, local banks will have to set aside 90% of foreign investors' new deposits as reserves, a leap from the current level of 9.775%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also raised its benchmark interest rate by 0.125 percentage point to 1.625%, the third increase this year, as it seeks to normalize lending costs and cool a sizzling property market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Perng Fai-nan said inflation will likely accelerate next year.\par \par \uc2 Also Thursday, Taiwan's financial regulator said it will inspect banks' use of foreign funds to determine whether there has been speculative trading in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had found "unusual" trading strategies at a small number of banks. "Over the past few days, a small number of authorized \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  banks have targeted specific times of the day to sell off large quantities of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 It isn't unusual for Asian central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when volatility in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises. Many have taken regulatory steps in recent months to try to slow capital inflows and make their banking systems more resilient to movements in foreign funds.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday that it would increase the amount of reserves commercial banks must hold at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  against foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits, among other steps. Also Wednesday, South Korea said it would announce lower ceilings on banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward positions in January.\par \par \uc2  - Joy Shaw in Shanghai, Min-Jeong Lee in Seoul and Ankur Relia in Kuala Lumpur contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2010 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110101e6cv00231\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
