\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Malaysia's Interest Rates Accommodative - Zeti\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Dezember 2010\par 08:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds more comments from governor, background)\par \par \uc2 By K.P. Lee\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zeti Akhtar Aziz said Thursday that interest rates in the Southeast Asian country were at an appropriate level, despite a rate increase in neighbouring Thailand a day earlier.\par \par \uc2 "Our assessment is that interest rates are at an appropriate level at this point in time given the outlook for inflation and the outlook for growth," Zeti said when asked if Malaysia would follow suit. She was speaking at an event in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday surprised the markets by raising its rate by 25 basis points to 2.0%, the third increase this year, citing potential threats to the economy due to inflation running above policy interest rates. With inflation at 2.8% in November, the Thailand authority said that real interest rates were negative, which could distort market mechanisms.\par \par \uc2 Early last month, \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  in its last rate-setting meeting of the current year kept its policy rate unchanged at 2.75%, after having raised rates by a total of 75 basis points in three increases earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 Inflationary pressures in Malaysia have remained benign over the last few months, and are expected to remain that way going forward, economists says, the majority of whom don't expect any rate hikes in the first half of 2011. In October, consumer prices in Malaysia rose 2.0% from a year earlier, compared with market expectations of 1.9%.\par \par \uc2 On the issue of capital controls, Zeti said any moves to curb capital flows should be implemented internationally or regionally. "I do not think any country can (introduce capital controls) successfully without causing instability to others."\par \par \uc2 The fast-growing economies in Southeast Asia have drawn a surge of capital from slower-growth areas seeking higher returns, fuelling concerns about creation of asset bubbles, stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that undercut export competitiveness and instability should the inflows suddenly reverse course.\par \par \uc2 Zeti maintained that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to maintain "orderly conditions." She said the ringgit will continue to strengthen in line with fundamentals, but the bank won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise is gradual. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence underlying trends," she added.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was trading at MYR3.1455 at 0700 GMT, down from MYR3.1500 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 -By K.P. Lee; Dow Jones Newswires; 603-2026-1233; kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com [ 02-12-10 0720GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101202e6c2000gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
