ybank  and planters \uc2 Sime Darby\uc2  <SIME.KL and \uc2 KL Kepong\uc2   led the market.  * Investors showed unusual caution on Tuesday, leaving U.S. stocks little changed before the potential market tumult of next week's U.S. elections and likely announcement of more stimulus from the Federal Reserve. [.N]  * Oil rose slightly, hovering above $82 a barrel on Tuesday, as rising U.S. consumer confidence figures were offset by a firming dollar and expectations of a boost in U.S. crude inventories.[O/R]  * For global market news, click on [MKTS/GLOB]  *  Malaysian palm oil futures eased on Tuesday on profit taking due to a firmer dollar, but losses were limited by strong Chinese demand for soybeans for crushing into vegetable oils. [POI/]  * To see Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regular money market tenders issued at around 0930 local please click on the following link {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fast.bnm.gov.my/fastweb/public/MainPage.do?mode=MAIN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fast.bnm.gov.my/fastweb/public/MainPage.do?mode=MAIN}}}\uc2   * To see Islamic finance stories from Malaysia and elsewhere click on [ID:nISLAMIC]  * For Malaysian stock recommendations hit <.KL> or [MY-RCH] \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------------------MARKET SNAPSHOT @ 2309 GMT ------------\par                     INSTRUMENT   LAST       PCT CHG   NET\par CHG S&P 500             <.SPX>       1185.64         0%    \par 0.020 USD/JPY             <JPY=>       81.37       -0.04%   \par -0.030 10-YR US TSY YLD    <US10YT=RR>  2.6448          --    \par 0.000 SPOT GOLD           <XAU=>       1342.76      0.30%    \par 4.060 US CRUDE            <CLc1>       82.42       -0.16%   \par -0.130 DOW JONES           <.DJI>       11169.46     0.05%     \par 5.41 ASIA ADRS           <.BKAS>      132.89      -0.57%    \par -0.76\par ------------------------------------------------------------- \par   FOR REALTIME MALAYSIAN ECONOMIC INDICATORS, HIT <ECONMY>\par \f28 \p