n signs of recovery. Unless there is any further negative development, the current stimulus is already producing results...We are very pleased private consumption is expanding and at the same time, there is some recovery in investment activity," she said.\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian economy shrank 3.9% on year in the second quarter of this year, but Zeti had earlier indicated that the economy may likely improve in the third quarter and turn positive in the fourth.\par \par \uc2 -By K.P. Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; (603) 2026 1233; kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com [ 20-10-09 0545GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091020e5ak000cv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
