\par\par \b \uc2 Malaysia-Market factors to watch July 21\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2009\par 01:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR, July 21 (Reuters) - Following is a list of events in Malaysia as well as news stories and press reports which may influence financial markets.\par \par \uc2 (Reuters News welcomes your feedback and for any queries please contact David Chance in Kuala Lumpur editorial on +603 2333 8033 or via email at david.chance@thomsonreuters.com or on Reuters messaging david.chance.reuters.com@reuters.net)\par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING IN MALAYSIA, ALL TIMES LOCAL FOLLOWED BY GMT\par \par \uc2 (The inclusion of diary items does not necessarily mean that Reuters will cover the event)\par \par \uc2 - Reuters issues June CPI poll <MYCPI=ECI>.\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Sime Darby\uc2  launches Safe City Initiative campaign at 9.30am (0130).\par \par \uc2 - Press conference by Axis Reit Managers on second quarter unaudited results at 10.00am (0200). MARKET SNAPSHOTS * Malaysia's benchmark FTSE Bursa KLCI ended Monday up 1.64 percent at 1,139.25 points, its highest since Aug. 5, led by financials and big caps on optimism over quarterly earnings. [.KLSE] * Technical indicators have confirmed a breakout and the index may continue to climb towards the next resistance levels at 1,150 and 1,163 points, said dealers at a leading Malaysian brokerage. * U.S. stocks jumped on Monday, driving the S&P 500 to an eight-month closing high, after \uc2 CIT Group Inc\uc2  was thrown a lifeline to avoid bankruptcy, and investors bet corporate America would log another strong set of earnings this week.[.N] * Oil rose on Monday as optimism about a potential global economic recovery lifted markets and expectations of a turnaround in fuel demand.[O/R] * For global market news, click on [MKTS/GLOB] * Malaysian crude palm oil futures rose 1.8 percent on Monday, extending the previous week's gains as Asian festival demand strengthened and other vegetable oil markets gained. [POI/] * To see Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regular money market tenders issued at around 0930 local please click on the following link {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fast.bnm.gov.my/fastweb/public/MainPage.do?mode=MAIN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fast.bnm.gov.my/fastweb/public/MainPage.do?mode=MAIN}}}\uc2  * To see the top Islamic finance stories from Malaysia and \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par elsewhere click on [ID:nISLAMIC] -------------------MARKET\par SNAPSHOT @ 23:10 GMT --------------\par                    INSTRUMENT   LAST     PCT CHG  NET CHG\par  S&P 500           <.SPX>       951.13   1.14%    10.750\par  USD/JPY           <JPY=>       94.07   -0.15%    -0.140\par  10-YR US TSY YLD  <US10YT=RR>  3.612    --        0.000\par  SPOT GOLD         <XAU=>       $950.00  0.17%     1.650\par  US CRUDE          <CLc1>       $64.54   0.88%     0.560\par  DOW JONES         <.DJI>       8848.15  1.19%    104.21\par  ASIA ADRS         <.BKAS>      112.23   2.59%     2.83\par ------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FOR MALAYSIAN ECONOMIC INDICATORS, CLICK ON [ID:nKLR424881] FOR REALTIME MALAYSIAN ECONOMIC INDICATORS, HIT <ECONMY> KEY GLOBAL ECONOMIC NEWS, SEE [TOP/MACRO] TOP NEWS ON ASIAN COMPANIES [TOP/EQA] FOR ECONOMIC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RELATED NEWS, HIT [FXNEWS] FOR WHAT INVESTORS ARE SAYING ABOUT DEALS [DEALTALK/] STOCKS - BUY OR SELL? [BUYSELL/] IN THE NEWS REUTERS MALAYSIA (Click on [MY-RTRS]) >Malaysia's Astro fails to detail plans [ID:nKLR425597] >Public Bank eyes 14-15 pct FY09' loan growth [ID:nKLR221818] >Malaysia \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par death may raise ethnic unease       [ID:nKLR474450] >Bursa\par Malaysia Q2 net profit up 22.3 pct     [ID:nKLR209429]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 >Indonesia TV identifies Jakarta bomb 