\par\par \b \uc2 Fitch Revises S Korea Rating Outlook To Negative From Positive\b0\par\par\uc2 927 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2008\par 01:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Corrected November 9, 2008 20:31 ET (01:31 GMT) [ 10-11-08 0007GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings-Hong Kong/Singapore-10 November 2008: This announcement clarifies the version issued earlier today to highlight that the Outlook on Malaysia's Long-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Issuer Default Rating is Stable. The correct version is as follows:\par \par \uc2 Fitch Ratings has today revised Korea's rating Outlook to Negative from Stable and the Outlook on Malaysia's Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Issuer Default Rating to Stable from Positive. At the same time, Fitch has affirmed the sovereign ratings with Stable Outlooks for China, Taiwan, and Thailand. India's Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Issuer Default rating (IDR) at 'BBB-' (BBB minus) is also affirmed with a Stable Outlook, and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  'BBB-' (BBB minus) IDR is affirmed with a Negative Outlook. All ratings are listed at the end of this announcement.\par \par \uc2 These rating actions follow the conclusion of a global review of the sovereign ratings of 17 major investment-grade emerging market economies conducted in response to the profound deterioration in the global economic and financial outlook.\par \par \uc2 "The revision to Korea's Outlook reflects concerns that the de-leveraging of the banking system may contribute to an erosion of the sovereign's external credit strengths, especially if it were accompanied by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the exchange rate," said James McCormack, head of Asia sovereigns at Fitch.\par \par \uc2 Fitch notes hat the authorities had responded quickly and in a focused manner to the funding distress of the banking system, with a comprehensive package of measures, including a USD30bn foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap facility and a USD100bn guarantee programme for new bank debt. Though potential external financing needs are large - a forecast current account deficit (plus outflows of net FDI) for next year of USD35bn plus short-term and liquid foreign liabilities estimated at USD176bn - external financing and liquidity concerns remain moderate given still sizeable Bank of Korea (BoK) \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of USD212bn at end-October 2008. The BoK also has access to a USD30bn \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap arrangement with the US Federal Reserve and other swap arrangements that are currently being discussed with the People's \uc2 Bank of China\uc2  and the Bank of Japan. Even so, the fiscal and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  cost of funding the 'de-leveraging' of the banking system against the backdrop of a sharp slowdown in the economy and deterioration in bank asset quality could erode Korea's external credit strengths, especially if the BoK engages in less targeted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In revising the Outlook on \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Stable, Fitch took into account the likely impact on the balance of payments of lower oil and other commodity prices, as well as the deterioration in external demand conditions for electronics exports. Malaysia is one of Asia's more open economies and the region's only significant net oil exporter.\par \par \uc2 To accompany today's global review, the Sovereign group will host a teleconference at 15:00 GMT/ 10:00 EST to discuss the review in further detail. A full list of rating actions and associated rationales are detailed in a special report, 'Rating Review of Emerging Markets', now available at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Teleconference details:\par \par \uc2 Date: Monday 10 November Time: 15:00 GMT; 10:00 ESTDial in numbers: UK Toll: +44 (0) 1452 565 508US Toll Free: +1 866 966 9449 Conference ID: 72232573\par \par \uc2 Replay (available until midnight on13 November): UK Toll: +44 (0) 1452 55 00 00US Toll Free: + 1 866 247 4222Replay pass code: 72232573#\par \par \uc2 South Korea:Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'A+'; Outlook revised to Negative from StableLong-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'AA'; Outlook revised to Negative from Stable Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'F1'Country Ceiling: affirmed at 'AA'\par \par \uc2 Malaysia:Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'A-' (A minus); Outlook revised to Stable from PositiveLong-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'A+'; Outlook Stable Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'F2'Country Ceiling: affirmed at 'A'\par \par \uc2 China:Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'A+'; Outlook StableLong-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'AA-' (AA minus); Outlook StableShort-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'F1'Country Ceiling: affirmed at 'A+'\par \par \uc2 Taiwan:Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'A+'; Outlook StableLong-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'AA'; Outlook StableShort-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'F1'Country Ceiling: affirmed at 'AA'\par \par \uc2 Thailand:Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'BBB+'; Outlook StableLong-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'A'; Outlook StableShort-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'F2'Country Ceiling: affirmed at 'A-'(A minus)\par \par \uc2 India:Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'BBB-' (BBB minus); Outlook StableLong-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'BBB-' (BBB minus); Outlook Negative Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  IDR: affirmed at 'F3'Country Ceiling: affirmed at 'BBB-' (BBB minus)\par \par \uc2 Contacts: James McCormack, Hong Kong, +852 2263 9925/ james.mccormack@fitchratings.com.\par \par \uc2 Media Relations: Shivani Sundralingam, Singapore, Tel: + 65 6796 7215, Email: shivani.sundralingam@fitchratings.com.\par \par \uc2 Fitch's rating definitions and the terms of use of such ratings are available on the agency's public site, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.fitchratings.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.fitchratings.com}}}\uc2 . Published ratings, criteria and methodologies are available from this site, at all times. Fitch's code of conduct, confidentiality, conflicts of interest, affiliate firewall, compliance and other relevant policies and procedures are also available from the 'Code of Conduct' section of this site. [ 10-11-08 1016GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081110e4ba0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
