\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asians supported by c.banks as risks rise\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 2008\par 07:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Sept 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks in Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  supported their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday after fears over \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 ' ability to raise capital stoked a fresh round of risk aversion and selling of Asian stocks.\par \par \uc2 Trading was however subdued as market participants waited for Lehman to report its quarterly results ahead of the U.S. stock market open. The stock plunged 45 percent overnight on fears it would fail to raise the funds it needs to survive.\par \par \uc2 But as stock markets globally fell and the dollar gained against the euro <EUR=>, it was obvious that the relief provided by Washington's bailout of mortgage giants \uc2 Fannie Mae\uc2  and \uc2 Freddie Mac\uc2  this week was wearing off.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's measure of Asia Pacific stocks excluding Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> fell 1 percent.\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee <INR=IN> fell to 45 per dollar, its weakest in nearly two years.\par \par \uc2 Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of selling dollars to defend the ringgit <MYR=> after it fell to 3.47 per dollar, its weakest in a year.\par \par \uc2 "They know that risk aversion trades are back in the market," said a trader in Kuala Lumpur. He said the Malaysian authorities would be keen to stop the ringgit from reaching 3.50, a level that could psychologically turn the market more bearish. "Also, they are trying to detach the political risk from the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so that's why their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a bit more aggressive these days," he said.\par \par \uc2 Political tensions have risen in Malaysia where opposition leader Anwar Ibrahim has said he will win over sufficient government legislators and take over from the ruling coalition this month.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the beleaguered Korean won <KRW=> won some respite from the heavy selling that has driven it down 14 percent this year, mainly on concerns over capital flight from the country.\par \par \uc2 It rose to near 1,088 per dollar, helped by selling of dollars by the authorities. [nSEO281709]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at   0458 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.16         106.82       -0.32\par  Sing dlr        1.4311         1.4349       +0.27\par  Taiwan dlr      31.865         31.872       +0.02\par  Korean won     1088.20        1094.75       +0.60\par  Baht             34.60          34.51       -0.26\par  Peso             46.80          46.82       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9325.00        9315.00       -0.11\par  Rupee            45.03          44.82       -0.46\par  Ringgit         3.4565         3.4470       -0.27\par  Yuan            6.8390         6.8381       -0.01\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       107.16         111.33       +3.89\par  Sing dlr        1.4311         1.4382       +0.50\par  Taiwan dlr      31.865         32.443       +1.81\par  Korean won     1088.20         935.70      -14.01\par  Baht             34.60          33.68       -2.66\par  Peso             46.80          41.28      -11.79\par  Rupiah         9325.00        9390.00       +0.70\par  Rupee            45.03          39.41      -12.47\par  Ringgit         3.4565         3.3050       -4.38\par  Yu