\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  Only For Orderly  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt\b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2008\par 07:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor's comments on inflation)\par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--Bank Negara Malaysia Governor Zeti Akhtar Aziz said Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "continues to monitor" the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and that it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when necessary to maintain orderly market conditions.\par \par \uc2 She also said the current weakness in the ringgit, which fell to its lowest this year against the U.S. dollar Monday, reflects the dollar's recent broad strength against many \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we undertake is to maintain orderly market conditions; that is our priority," Zeti said.\par \par \uc2 "We will not be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to affect the underlying trend of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," she said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the past one week by selling the dollar to slow the weakening of the ringgit.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to MYR3.3200 Monday, its highest this year, compared with MYR3.2630 a week ago. The greenback has risen against major and regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently largely due to falling crude oil prices.\par \par \uc2 On the economy, Zeti said Malaysia's inflation rate, which hit a 26-year high of 7.7% in June, will moderate in 2009 on a likely slowdown in economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "Moderation in growth will have some dampening effect on inflation...we are already seeing commodity prices retrace," she said.\par \par \uc2 Zeti said the high inflation experienced recently was part of "the first-round effects."\par \par \uc2 "What we have to monitor is the second-round effects, and with the moderation in growth, we expect that inflation will moderate next year, particularly in the second half of the year," she said.\par \par \uc2 - K.P. Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; 603-2168 4273; kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com [ 11-08-08 0504GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080811e48b0006s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
