\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - East Asia   \b0\par\par\uc2 1,139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2007\par 03:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 - 0104 GMT [Dow Jones]--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in East Asia today:   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par               Immediate Range   Larger Range \par     USD/CNY   7.5809-7.6075    7.5605-7.6123 \par     USD/HKD   7.7967-7.8199    7.7900-7.8258 \par     USD/KRW   938.70-952.00    935.10-955.00 \par     USD/TWD   32.890-33.170    32.750-33.430 \par     USD/SGD   1.5247-1.5427    1.5158-1.5500 \par     USD/MYR   3.4900-3.5185    3.4750-3.5310 \par     USD/THB    31.55-33.38      30.90-34.47 \par     USD/PHP        --               -- \par     USD/IDR     9360-9500        9330-9560 \par  \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent high and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)   \par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- has downward bias after Fed surprised markets by cutting discount rate by 50 bps to 5.75% from 6.25% Friday in effort to add liquidity to market. Citing rising risks to economy, Fed has effectively moved to easing bias; some economists say Fed may lower fed funds rate at Sep 18 FOMC meeting. USD selling by some exporters helped to push up CNY late Friday afternoon. Central parity was set higher for 6th consecutive session at 7.6003, vs 7.5981 Thursday, and above psychologically important 7.6 level for first time since July 9. Shenzhen-based trader says USD to trade in CNY7.5900-CNY7.6100 range this week. Dow Jones technical analysis shows USD/CNY faces immediate resistance at 7.6075 (Friday high), followed by 7.6123 (July 6 high). Immediate support at 7.5809 (July 30 high), next at 7.5605 (Aug 9 low).   \par \par \uc2 USD/HKD -- has downward bias after Fed's 50bp discount rate cut Friday, likely fed funds rate cut Sep 18. Most US money markets remain in full risk-aversion mode despite Fed's action. HKD rose sharply against USD Friday as investors unwound their carry-trade positions to reduce risks amid continued tightening in global liquidity; some traders expect USD to fall more vs HKD in near term on further unwinding of carry trades. HK jobless rate likely to edge down in 2H to around 4.0% by year-end vs 4.2% tipped in 3 months to July, according to Dow Jones poll; data due at 0815 GMT today. Dow Jones technical analysis shows USD/HKD has initial support at 7.7967 (Friday low), then 7.7900 (psychological support). Immediate resistance at 7.8199 (Friday's high), followed by 7.8258 (Tuesday's high).   \par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- downward bias. Easing concerns over yen-carry trade unwinding helping Kospi rebound strongly today, after recent massive selling in local shares by foreign investors. Local bank dealer says retreat in JPY/KRW cross rate, and export settlements poised heavily around 950 level, may further help possible KRW rise today. USD/KRW faces immediate resistance at 952.20 (Friday's high), followed by psychological 955.00. Initial support at 938.70 (Thursday's low), next at 935.10 (May high).   \par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- has downward bias. USD/TWD ended lower Friday on exporters' demand for local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defense of TWD; \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at session end, suspected of selling US$250 million in last half hour of trade, say traders. Pair faces immediate resistance at 33.17 (June 18 high), followed by 33.43 (May high). Initial support at 32.89 (55-day average), then 32.75 (July 11 high).   \par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- has downward bias. MAS "appeared to have stepped in" Friday as trade-weighted SGD dropped 1% below undisclosed policy band, says  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  in note to clients. Adds SGD "well in the weak side of its policy band" but if contagion continues to hit Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , SGD may feel "limited impact" as possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  provides shield. Dow Jones reported S$200 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, citing traders. USD/SGD faces immediate resistance at 1.5427 (Friday high), followed by psychological 1.5500. Minor support at 1.5247 (55-day average), next at 1.5158 (last Monday's low).   \par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- has downward bias. \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday, but USD/MYR plowed higher: Bank Negara sold $500 million at 3.5130, about $300 million at 3.5180, just off March high of 3.5185 (3.5080 late Thursday), says KL trader. Data Friday showed Malaysia's June manufacturing sales +2.6% on year vs May's restated +2.9%. SCB expects MYR, PHP and SGD to strengthen again as ASEAN fundamentals remain strong.  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  has downgraded its 2007 U.S. GDP growth forecast but upped its global projection because of higher expectations for Asia. USD/MYR faces immediate resistance at 3.5185 (March high), followed by major resistance at 55-week moving average, now at 3.5310. Initial support at 3.4900 (June high), followed by 3.4750 (Aug 1 high).   \par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- has downward bias. Equity-linked outflows pushed pair up to session high of 34.69 Friday before selling by exporters trimmed gains. Thai voters approved new military-drafted constitution yesterday, but large number of "no" votes suggest former Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra remains a political force; full official results expected later today. Public endorsement of constitution could pave way for elections in December, local bourse likely to rally, possibly bring back some inflows. SCB expects MYR, PHP and SGD to strengthen again as ASEAN fundamentals remain strong. Offshore USD/THB faces immediate resistance at 33.38 (200-day moving average), followed by 34.47 (March 26 high). Minor support at 31.55 (Aug 13 high), followed by 30.90 (July 26 high).   \par \par \uc2 USD/PHP - Philippines market shut today due to holiday.   \par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- to consolidate with downward bias. Indonesia market was shut Friday due to holiday. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  thought to have sold more than $400 million Thursday through state banks as foreign investors exited Indonesian markets. SCB remains neutral on IDR on expectations Bank Indonesia to maintain its dovish policy slant, could cut rates to 7% next year. Dow Jones technical analysis shows USD/IDR testing immediate resistance psychological 9500, followed by 9560 (June 2006 high). Immediate support at 9360 (Wednesday low), followed by 9330 (Aug 13 low).   \par \par \uc2 (Alfred Yeo, alfred.yeo@dowjones.com)   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Murugesan Suppayyan   \par \par \uc2 Dow Jones CommentaryPlus Web site:   {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djcommentaryplus.com/acs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djcommentaryplus.com/acs  }}}\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 20-08-07 0104GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020070820e38k00003\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
