\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-FACTBOX-How central banks have acted to inject funds   \b0\par\par\uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2007\par 19:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with no action from Fed)   \par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT, Aug 14 (Reuters) - Global central banks are withdrawing much of the extra cash they have injected into banking systems to calm panicky credit since last Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Below is a list of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions since the credit markets upheaval turned nasty last week.   \par \par \uc2 EUROPEAN \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Aug 9 - 94.8 billion euros ($129.8 billion) in a one-day tender on Thursday, the largest amount ever.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 10 - 61.05 billion euros ($83.61 billion) in a three-day tender on Friday to cover the weekend,   \par \par \uc2 Aug 13 - 47.67 billion euros ($65.29 billion) in one-day money on Monday   \par \par \uc2 Aug 14 - 7.7 billion in one-day money on Tuesday. The ECB also added an extra 73.5 billion euros in one-week money more than its estimated liquidity needs for banks during its main refinancing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Trichet also issued a statement on Tuesday calling for investors to stay composed composure in face of market volatility and a repricing of risk.   \par \par \uc2 The ECB's injections exceed those that it flooded into markets immediately after the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks on the United States. At that time, 69.3 billion euro in overnight money was allocated on Sept. 12, 2001, followed by 40.5 billion euros the next day.   \par \par \uc2 U.S. FEDERAL RESERVE   \par \par \uc2 Aug 9 - $24 billion during its regular market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , only slightly above the usual allocation.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 10 - Added $38 billion through three separate repurchase agreements, its biggest single-day cash injection since Sept. 19, 2001. The repos brought down the federal funds rate, the cost of overnight loans between banks, to the Fed's target rate of 5.25 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 13 - Added $2 billion of temporary reserves to the banking system through overnight repurchasing agreements.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 14 - The Fed took the unusual step of refraining from an open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 9:30 a.m. (1330 GMT), when daily \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are usually conducted. In an earlier statement, the Fed said it was evaluating whether or not to conduct an \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  at that time and said it stood ready to conduct additional \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day as needed.   \par \par \uc2 BANK OF JAPAN   \par \par \uc2 Aug 10 - Added 1.0 trillion yen ($8.45 billion) at its regular money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday after a slight rise in the benchmark overnight call rate, the highest amount in about six weeks. Traders said the amount was at the higher end of market expectations, but was not a major surprise.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 13 - Added 600 billion yen ($5.1 billion) into the banking system in a one-week \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Aug 14 - Drained 1.6 trillion yen ($13.6 billion) in two \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 BANK OF ENGLAND   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of England said banks hit by tough credit conditions could use its emergency lending facility, which is routinely available and priced at 100 basis points above the bank's 5.75 percent policy rate.   \par \par \uc2 BANK OF CANADA   \par \par \uc2 Aug 9 - Injected C$1.64 billion ($1.55 billion) on Thursday, saying it was in contact with other central banks on the global situation and stood ready to add money as needed.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 10 - Injected a total of C$1.685 billion ($1.605 billion)   \par \par \uc2 Aug 13 - Injected C$670 million.   \par \par \uc2 THE RESERVE BANK OF AUSTRALIA   \par \par \uc2 Aug 10 - The RBA added more than twice the usual amount of money into the banking system, injecting A$4.95 billion ($4.19 billion).   \par \par \uc2 Aug 14 - The RBA added A$2.6 billion ($2.2 billion) in its regular morning money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slightly higher than average.   \par \par \uc2 SWISS NATIONAL BANK   \par \par \uc2 Aug 9/10 - The SNB offered banks money at a below-market rate of 2.6 percent on Thursday and Friday, adding a total of 3.1 billion Swiss francs ($2.57 billion) <CHF=>. It since has started to drain the extra liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 Aug 13/14 - Traders said the SNB drained liquidity as overnight rates remained low after the previous week's liquidity-providing actions.   \par \par \uc2 CENTRAL BANKS OF \b \highlight22\uc2 MALAYSIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , INDONESIA, PHILIPPINES   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Asian central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling U.S. dollars. Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Zeti Akhtar Aziz said on Monday there was sufficient liquidity in its financial system, but that it was monitoring the situation.   \par \par \uc2 BANK OF KOREA   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it was ready to add funds to markets if needed.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  OF NORWAY   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday's loan of 45 billion crowns ($7.80 billion) gave ample liquidity to banks and it would continue to ensure orderly \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market.   \par \par \uc2 For a wrap on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, please double-click on [ID:nL14733872]   \par \par \uc2 CENTRALBANKS/ (FACTBOX) (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|ABX|BNX|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070814e38e001hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
