\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupee powers to 9-year high, won at 16-week peak   \b0\par\par\uc2 838 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 April 2007\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 23 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee extended gains to a nine-year high versus the dollar on Monday, outpacing most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on strong capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2  Foreign buying in South Korea's equity market helped push the won <KRW=> to a 16-week high, while the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> tested last week's nine-year peaks before suspected dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down.   \par \par \uc2  Asia's other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  nudged lower, with a rally in the yen encouraging investors to unwind yen carry trades for now. Most regional units have benefited from such trades that involve selling the low-yielding yen to fund investments in assets that offer a higher yield.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee <INR=IN> briefly rose to 41.56 per dollar, its highest level since May 1998, helped by a rally in the stock market <.BSESN> and news on Friday that India's annual inflation rate unexpectedly jumped back above 6 percent in early April.   \par \par \uc2  It has gained more than 6 percent this year, putting it clearly ahead as Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. This month alone the rupee has jumped 4 percent.   \par \par \uc2  "Everybody's looking at the rupee and there has been a sudden surge of interest in the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said BNP Paribas \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Thio Chin Loo.   \par \par \uc2  "People are searching for value in Asia and the fact that the Indian rupee hadn't moved that much, so traders are looking at the opportunities there."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  CAUTION   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb rupee strength forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give up some of its gains.   \par \par \uc2  And elsewhere in the region, dealers remained watchful of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks.   \par \par \uc2  A trader in Kuala Lumpur said \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after the ringgit strengthened to 3.42 per dollar -- matching a nine-year high set at the end of last week.   \par \par \uc2  "I think they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) were in the market at 3.42," said the trader. "Given the strong sentiment towards Malaysia, we will break 3.42 soon."   \par \par \uc2  The won rose to 925.10 per dollar, its highest level since Jan. 3, amid strong foreign buying of Korean shares.   \par \par \uc2  The benchmark KOSPI <.KS11> share index hit a record high on Monday and foreign investors were net buyers for a seventh consecutive session, bringing their total during that period to a net 1.2 trillion won ($1.30 billion) worth.   \par \par \uc2  Still, the upbeat won sentiment was tempered slightly by wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  On Friday, South Korea warned speculators against piling borrowed foreign funds into the won, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said monitoring of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had shown excessive speculative trading of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by some companies.   \par \par \uc2  "We suspect this reflects genuine worries about the possibility of a new surge in exporter selling taking dollar/won still lower," ABN AMRO \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Shahab Jalinoos said in a note to clients.   \par \par \uc2  "Exporters such as shipbuilders have been less active in the market than in 2006, but in recent days their presence has been noted."   \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> touched a fresh six-year high at 47.43 per dollar before declining to a session low at 47.67 as investors booked profits on recent peso gains.   \par \par \uc2  A trader in Manila said he did not think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped into the market to curb the peso, although it has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last few weeks.   \par \par \uc2  "We hit 47.43 and then there was some profit-taking and some short-covering," he said. "It looks like some people were looking to reverse the market."    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0803 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       118.30         118.69       +0.33\par  Sing dlr        1.5120         1.5102       -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr      33.166         33.136       -0.09\par  Korean won      925.80         927.40       +0.17\par  Baht             34.81          34.77       -0.11\par  Peso             47.66          47.43       -0.48\par  Rupiah         9090.00        9086.00       -0.04\par  Rupee            41.68          41.76       +0.20\par  Ringgit         3.4215         3.4200       -0.04\par  Yuan            7.7233         7.7197       -0.05\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    P