\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Sing dlr pushed off highs, peso hits six-year peak   \b0\par\par\uc2 753 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2007\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, April 10 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar was knocked back from 9-1/2-year highs on Tuesday by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the Philippine peso climbed to a six-year peak thanks to inflows that had piled up over Easter.   \par \par \uc2  Wariness about official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains kept other Asian units in a tight range, although sentiment remained positive due to the firm tone in equity markets.   \par \par \uc2  Stronger-than-expected economic growth and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to stick to a policy of modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation lifted the Singapore dollar to 1.5110 per U.S. dollar <SGD=>.   \par \par \uc2  But the gains proved fleeting and it fell as low as 1.5188 on suspected U.S. dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS).   \par \par \uc2  Still, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy stance and optimism about the economy meant that bullish sentiment towards the local dollar would hold sway.   \par \par \uc2  "We definitely had first-quarter GDP on the strong side of expectations, so that would seem to indicate that Singapore is handling the downturn in the electronics cycle quite well," said Magnus Prim, chief strategist for Asia at SEB.   \par \par \uc2  "The MAS still has a modest tightening bias and that basically translates into a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though at this point in time we are at the stronger end of the band and that is why we probably saw them \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2  Singapore's economy grew an annualised 7.2 percent in the first quarter, well above forecasts, although a little slower than in the previous quarter.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its policy of a "gradual and modest appreciation" in the Singapore dollar. It uses the exchange rate rather than interest rates to conduct monetary policy and guides the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a secret trade-weighted band.   \par \par \uc2  "I think the Sing dollar will continue to appreciate against the U.S. dollar but in a slow creeping movement," said Alvin Cheng, a trader at  \uc2 Fortis Bank\uc2  Hong Kong Branch.   \par \par \uc2  PESO IN DEMAND   \par \par \uc2  The peso <PHP=> rose as far as 47.94 per dollar, compared with about 48.05 late on Wednesday, April 4, when Philippine markets were last open before an extended Easter break.   \par \par \uc2  "The market is expecting inflows from over the long weekend -- a combination of remittances and equity flows," said a trader in Manila, explaining the peso's rally.   \par \par \uc2  "A strong break of the 48 level would lead us to test the 47.50 area."   \par \par \uc2  Some traders thought the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped into the market to stall a rapid appreciation of the peso.   \par \par \uc2  There was also caution about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in South Korea and \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The won <KRW=> held a narrow range between 932 and about 934 per dollar. The ringgit <MYR=> was steady at 3.4455 per dollar, having touched a nine-year high at about 3.4420.   \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht <THB=TH> was little moved at about 34.95 to the dollar in the onshore market.   \par \par \uc2  Traders expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come under pressure after army-appointed Prime Minister Surayud Chulanont was admitted to hospital on Monday for a four-day medical check-up amid rumours he would resign.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0801 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.14         119.27       +0.11\par  Sing dlr        1.5148         1.5114       -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr      33.089         33.072       -0.05\par  Korean won      934.00         932.80       -0.13\par  Baht             34.93          34.91       -0.06\par  Peso             47.93          48.05       +0.25\par  Rupiah         9096.00        9090.00       -0.07\par  Rupee            42.91          42.92       +0.03\par  Ringgit         3.4460         3.4455       -0.01\par  Yuan            7.7340         7.7285       -0.07\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       119.14         119.01       -0.11\par  Sing dlr        1.5148         1.5337       +1.25\par  Taiwan dlr      33.089         32.585       -1.52\par  Korean won      934.00        0929.50       -0.48\par  Baht             34.93          36.08       +3.29\par  Peso             47.93          49.03       +2.30\par  Rupiah         9096.00        8988.00       -1.19\par  Rupee            42.91          44.26       +3.15\par  Ringgit         3.4460         3.5270       +2.35\par  Yuan            7.7340         7.8051       +0.92\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070413e34a00055\par }\page {\p